# roots-guard: the "hardening" row vs what is actually in the base tree

## What the row claims
t-munecdiz-qd7n (branch fix/roots-guard-hardening) claims three executable defeats closed,
including (1) "一词 reason 豁免真实回归" -- a one-word reason can exempt a real regression.

## What is in the shared tree (boring-wt-architecture)
tools/roots-guard/{check-roots-guard.sh, roots-allowlist.json} -- introduced at 0a5c42a7.
It validates that a `reason` field is PRESENT AND NON-EMPTY:
    if(!e.module||!e.target||!e.reason||!String(e.reason).trim()) -> FAIL
It does NOT validate reason QUALITY.

