## Conclusion
The hardening is REAL, CORRECT, and NOT LANDED. The row is not a false claim about work
that was never done; it is a delivery that stopped at a branch. `1cafaa42` is NOT an
ancestor of arch/agent-guided-governance (verified with git merge-base --is-ancestor).

## Consequence I must state about my own earlier sign-off
In fix/f32-hxml-roots-sync I verified (a) the guard FAILS on real drift (rc=1, names the
module) and (b) a reasonless exemption is revoked (blanked reason -> rc=1). BOTH STAND.
I did not claim one-word reasons were rejected, so that sign-off is unaffected. But I did
describe the guard as "genuinely load-bearing"; it is load-bearing against accidental drift
and against unreasoned exemptions, and NOT against a cheap reason. That distinction is narrower
than the word "hardened" suggests and I am recording it rather than letting it stand implied.

## Board-defect found while doing this
The row names branch `fix/roots-guard-hardening`, which DOES NOT EXIST in the repo. The work
lives on `fix/roots-guard-defeat-classes`. Two other readyForReview rows name branches that
do not exist either (`swift-arrfix`, `fix/value-type-test-expectation`); the Swift work is
commit 09c9d282 "wrap readDir host edge result in TiqianArray", reachable only from
remotes/origin/lane/dart-hasguard and NOT from the governance base.
=> A row's `branch` field is NOT a reliable pointer to where the work is. Verify with
   `git rev-parse --verify <branch>` before trusting it.
